rees\nStudentships & Scholarships\nEmployability\nInternational Students\nInformation for New Students\nSeminars & Events\nShow submenu for Seminars & Events\nUpcoming Seminars\nDurham Symposia\nCollingwood Lecture Series\nPascal Lecture Series\nDistinguished Lecture Series\nInternational Women's Day Talks\nBlack History Month Lectures\nResearch & Impact\nShow submenu for Research & Impact\nResearch Areas\nImpact\nFellowships\nEDI & Outreach\nShow submenu for EDI & Outreach\nEquality, Diversity & Inclusion\nOutreach\nResources\nWomen in Maths\nFirst-Generation Scholars\nDecolonisation\nPublic Engagement\nSchool Outreach\nWidening Participation\nCurrent Students & Staff\nShow submenu for Current Students & Staff\nUG Maths Students Area\nPGT Maths Students Area\nPGR Maths Students Area\nMaths Staff Area\nREF 2021 Result\nShow submenu for REF 2021 Result\nStudentships and Scholarships\nThere are a variety of funding opportunities available to support your postgraduate studies. PhD Studentships support students studying for a PhD, covering tuition fees and typically contributing to living expenses. Scholarships support students at all levels, including Master's students, and offer a range of financial support.\nPhD Studentships\nLearn more about PhD Studentships available in the Department of Mathematical Sciences.\nScholarships\nLearn more about Scholarships available in the Department of Mathematical Sciences.\nPhD Studentships\nLearn more about PhD Studentships available in the Department of Mathematical Sciences.\nScholarships\nLearn more about Scholarships available in the Department of Mathematical Sciences.\nPhD Studentships\nThe Department of Mathematical Sciences invites applications for fully-funded PhD Studentships across a wide range of research areas. Each year, the Department offers a number of funded positions and welcomes applications from highly motivated and talented candidates.\nThe available studentships will be finalised towards the end of Autumn, however studentships often include:\nEPSRC Doctoral Landscape Awards (DLA): Research in priority areas including Data Science, AI & Robotics, Health Sciences, Quantum & Advanced Sensing, Energy Futures, Molecular Sciences, and Critical Infrastructure. Collaborative projects with external partners encouraged.\nSTFC PhD Studentships: Research in areas covered by STFC's remit, including Particle Physics (Theory) and Astronomy, solar and planetary science.\nChina Scholarship Council (CSC) Scholarships: Open to applicants from Mainland China, supporting excellent doctoral research across the Faculty of Science.\nGlobal Grand Challenges Studentships: Focused on SDG13: Climate Action, addressing climate change and building a more resilient global future.\nDurham Doctoral Training Fellowships: Enable students to study for a PhD in one of the Department's leading Research Groups, while acquiring valuable teaching skills. These studentships typically include a one-year teaching position alongside a PhD studentship. The Fellow is assigned both a supervision team and a mentor from the Education & Pedagogy Group, who supports their teaching-related activities.\nMore information about PhD Studentships can be found here.\nFor eligibility, deadlines, and application enquiries, please read the area-specific information here or contact maths.postgraduate@durham.ac.uk.\nWe also support students applying for external funding and financial support. Please contact maths.postgraduate@durham.ac.uk before starting an application.\nScholarships\nA variety of Scholarships are available that can support you in your postgraduate studies. Click on the links below to explore the different possibilities and find out how to apply.\nPostgraduate Scholarships\nLearn more about all available postgraduate funding opportunities across the University.\nInternational Scholarships\nFind out more about International Scholarships\nAlumni Scholarships\nFind out more about the Alumni Fee Scholarship\nDiscover more\nResearch Degrees\nFind out more about Postgraduate Research Degrees in the Department of Mathematical Sciences.\nTaught Degrees\nFind out more about our Postgraduate Taught Degrees.\nResearch Degrees\nFind out more about Postgraduate Research Degrees in the Department of Mathematical Sciences.\nTaught Degrees\nFind out more about our Postgraduate Taught Degrees.\nContact Durham University\nAbout us\nDurham University on Bluesky\nDurham University on Twitter\nDurham University on Facebook\nDurham University on LinkedIn\nDurham University on YouTube\nDurham University on Instagram\nDurham University on TikTok\nThe University\nAbout us\nJobs\nContact us\nVisit us\nOur Colleges\nAcademic Departments\nCeremonies\nStatements and policies\nNotices\nStatement on Modern Slavery\nFreedom of expression\nWebsite accessibility\nStudent complaints and non-academic misconduct\nSafeguarding\nBusiness services\nHelping business\nAnalytical services\nGlobal Durham\nInternational Consortia\nResearch and partnerships\nUseful links\nLearn Ultra\nBanner Self-Service\nStaff directory\nTechnician Commitment\nDU Hub (Internal)\nIT help and support\nThe Palatine Centre\nDurham University\nStockton Road\nDurham\nDH1 3LE\nCharitable status\nDisclaimer\nTrading name\nCookie notice\nPrivacy notices\n\u00a92026 Durham University", "links": [["Skip to main content", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/departments/academic/mathematical-sciences/postgraduate-study/studentships-and-scholarships/#main-content"], ["", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/"], ["", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/"], ["Alumni", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/alumni/"], ["Library and Collections", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/departments/library/"], ["Business School", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/business/"], ["Things To Do", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/things-to-do/"], ["About us", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/about-us/"], ["How to contact us", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/about-us/how-to-contact-us/"], ["Study", "https://www.durham.ac.uk/study/"], ["Undergrad